      "content": "I see. So you're basically suggesting that more traditional or \"collectivist\" lifestyles are inherently harder to insure because they aren't as stable? \n\nIt's just an interesting angle because it seems to imply that the more \"community-focused\" someone is—which is often how people from certain ethnic or immigrant backgrounds live—the more \"volatile\" they are considered for a policy. Do you think our models could inadvertently penalize certain demographics just because their cultural norms involve more communal living or frequent gatherings?",
